    [BugFix] Unify DeepSeek V4 tensor parallel limits across hardware (#19240)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    A5 now supports tensor parallelism. Remove the hardware-specific
    DeepSeek V4 TP policy introduced in #18418 and use the same
    model-specific limits on all hardware families:
    
    - DeepSeek V4 Flash and V4.1 Flash: TP <= 8.
    - DeepSeek V4 Pro: TP <= 16.
    
    Remove the A5 single-rank restriction and the unused hardware policy
    enum/fields. Preserve the existing Model Runner V1 DSA-CP exception.
    This matches the updated release-branch behavior in #19203.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. A5 accepts DeepSeek V4 TP configurations up to the same
    model-specific limits as other hardware. All hardware families now use
    uniform TP8/TP16 validation. A release note fragment is included in this
    PR.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Updated the unit regression matrix for all hardware profiles and both
    runners: accept TP1, TP2, and the model limit; reject TP above that
    limit.
    - Preserved coverage for text-config aliases, the V1 DSA-CP exception,
    V2 with DSA-CP, and unrelated models.
    - Passed: cached pre-commit Ruff check and Ruff format check for the
    three changed Python files.
    - Passed: `py -3 -m py_compile vllm_ascend/platform.py
    vllm_ascend/device/hardware_profile.py tests/ut/test_platform.py`.
    - Passed: `git diff upstream/main HEAD --check`.
    - `bash format.sh ci` could not complete: pre-commit failed to install
    actionlint because Go dependency downloads from `proxy.golang.org` timed
    out. Workspace knowledge was queried; no applicable verified local fix
    was found. The focused Python lint/format checks passed.
    - Previous CI: pre-commit/mypy and both CPU UT lanes passed on the
    initial run. A later run failed during conftest import before tests ran:
    CI installed old vLLM `c4df37df`, then rebased Ascend onto a newer main
    snapshot importing `target_dependent_ar`.
    - Rebased onto main `b4c0a83fe`, which includes #18224 and updates the
    verified vLLM pin to `a98247ab`. The imported module exists at that pin.
    Re-ran focused lint, format, syntax, and whitespace checks successfully;
    fresh CI is pending.
    - NPU execution has not been performed locally.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [x] Boundary / edge-case coverage
    - [x] Regression test
    - [x] Error / failure path coverage
    - [x] Meaningful & reliable tests
    - [ ] Performance impact (configuration validation only)
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
